{"5:5":"hell -- Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\")","27:20":"grave -- Also; Proverbs 30:16, Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\").","11:5":"perfect -- (See Scofield \"1 Kings 8:61\").","11:25":"liberal soul -- See; 2 Corinthians 9:6-10.","11:28":"trusteth -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\").","28:25":"trust -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\"), Also; Proverbs 29:25.","31:11":"trust -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\").","31:30":"feareth -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")","9:10":"fear -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")","9:18":"hell -- Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\")","24:21":"fear -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")","8:1":"hell -- Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\")","8:13":"fear -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")","8:22":"The Lord possessed me -- That wisdom is more than the personification of an attribute of God, or of the will of God as best for man, but is a distinct adumbration of Christ, is sure to the devout mind. Proverbs 8:22-36; John 1:1-3; Colossians 1:17 can refer to nothing less than the Eternal Son of God.","19:23":"fear -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").","10:1":"foolish son -- A \"fool\" in Scripture is never a mentally deficient person, but rather one arrogant and self-sufficient; one who orders his life as if there were no God. See, for illustration, Luke 12:16-20. The rich man was not mentally deficient, but he was a \"fool\" because he supposed that his soul could live on the things in the barn, giving no thought to his eternal wellbeing.","10:27":"fear -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")","3:5":"trust -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\")","3:7":"fear -- Also; Proverbs 2:5 (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\")","15:11":"hell -- Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\"), Job 26:6; Psalms 139:8.","15:16":"fear -- Also; Proverbs 14:26, (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").","15:24":"hell -- Heb. \"Sheol,\" (See Scofield \"Habakkuk 2:5\")","15:33":"fear -- (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").","7:27":"hell -- Heb. \"Sheol,\" (S